description:
memory.rs:534-555 (and the same shape at memory.rs:967-1000 for the override) uses Vec::contains for every push:

  for rec in &entry.created {
      if !destroyed.contains(&rec.id) && !created.contains(&rec.id) {
          created.push(rec.id.clone());
      }
  }

contains is O(n) on Vec; nested in an outer iteration over entries this is O(window² × records_per_entry). For a 1000-entry change window with a few records each, the dedup is O(1M) Id comparisons (each requiring a String compare on Id's inner repr).

This is the kind of O(n²) that 'survives into production because test data is small' (Section 2 of the review prompt). The integration tests cover at most ~4 ids per /changes call — they never exercise the quadratic part.

Fix: replace the Vec::contains pattern with HashSet<&Id> or HashMap<&Id, fate_tag> to track which ids have been seen and what their fate is. Mail-server's IdFate approach (memory.rs:577-613) uses a HashMap and avoids the quadratic — propagating that algorithm here (per JMAP-826m.8) would fix this too.
